Description: allow wake for RPA devices when the kernel has LL Privacy
 BlueZ 5.72 only enables wake support for devices that use a resolvable
 private address when the kernel experimental feature "RPA resolution"
 (15c0a148-c273-11ea-b3de-0242ac130004) is on, because otherwise the device
 cannot be programmed in the controller accept list.
 Newer kernels (e.g. 7.0) no longer have that experimental feature: when the
 controller supports LL Privacy the kernel uses it automatically and reports
 MGMT_SETTING_LL_PRIVACY. Accept that setting as well, so Bluetooth LE
 keyboards and mice with privacy addresses can wake the host again.
 The check still refuses wake when neither is available.
Author: Zerun Wang <213201277+ZerunW@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: not-needed (upstream master dropped the check)
---
--- a/src/device.c
+++ b/src/device.c
@@ -1505,8 +1505,14 @@
 
+#ifndef MGMT_SETTING_LL_PRIVACY
+#define MGMT_SETTING_LL_PRIVACY		BIT(22)
+#endif
+
 void device_set_wake_support(struct btd_device *device, bool wake_support)
 {
 	if (device->rpa && !btd_adapter_has_exp_feature(device->adapter,
-						EXP_FEAT_RPA_RESOLUTION)) {
+						EXP_FEAT_RPA_RESOLUTION) &&
+			!btd_adapter_has_settings(device->adapter,
+						MGMT_SETTING_LL_PRIVACY)) {
 		warn("Unable to set wake_support without RPA resolution");
 		return;
 	}
